(:id "rust/R28" :state :unknown :note "the guard chain is not implemented in this leg's runtime: the plan entry carries ONE guard lane (guard/arg/argw) and no second conjoin lane (guard2/arg2/argw2) nor an offset+count pool of (guard, arg, argw) links, outermost first, so an arm inside an arm answers only the inner tag (docs/FIXED-FORM-ALGORITHM.md §4.1)")
(:id "rust/W6" :state :unknown :note "plan partition / split is not implemented: table_fixed_compile coalesces but never partitions the plan unguarded-first and no split index is stated (docs/FIXED-FORM-ALGORITHM.md §4.1, §4.4)")
(:id "rust/P1" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/rusttable/fixedroadmap_t08_test.go: TestFixedRoadmapRustT08WritesConformance/rust/P1") :tested-revision "445a8715e")
(:id "rust/W13" :state :unknown :note "layout+hash == C++ reference: proving it needs the reference's byte oracle (build/fixedform-corpus and the files the dump writes), and this job has no corpus and no sibling ../serialize runtime, so the reference cannot be built or run inside the wall; the clause's whole-file byte comparison lives in test/rust-fixedform/src/main.rs (round_trip!'s out == golden, reached by the_write)")
(:id "rust/P2" :state :unknown :note "write-read-write byte-identical: proving it needs a written record read back against the C++ reference's own bytes, which needs the sibling ../serialize runtime and the corpus this job does not have; the clause lives in test/rust-fixedform/src/main.rs the_write")
(:id "rust/R27" :state :unknown :note "the manifest is the wire (build/fixedform-corpus/manifest.txt is the single value oracle every leg reads to): the manifest is written by the C++ reference build, which this job cannot make (no sibling ../serialize runtime), so no test that reads it can run here")
(:id "rust/P3" :state :unknown :note "hostile bytes, sweep + sanitizer: the sweep is the harness's the_hostile_sweep (test/rust-fixedform/src/main.rs), which supplies hostile bytes and counts the three answers; it RUNS only against the corpus this job cannot build, and a text-grep of its source proves no clause")
(:id "rust/P4" :state :unknown :note "wrong plan goes red: the negative control is the harness's the_negative_controls (test/rust-fixedform/src/main.rs), which RUNS only against the corpus this job cannot build")
